      "CHRISTMASMARKET was minted by Nation Europa's Alsatian heritage exchange in Strasbourg — the city that has been running a Christmas market since 1570 and considers itself the original, the Christkindelsmärik, the market that all other markets are trying to be. The exchange minted it as the coin of the tradition that predates the nation-state, the euro, and the concept of a seasonal coin, but which would have minted one immediately if given the opportunity.",
