    origin:
      "GLUHWEIN was minted by Nation Europa's German Christmas market exchange on the evening the first Glühwein of the season was poured into a ceramic mug that cost more than the wine and was kept as a souvenir, because in Germany the mug deposit is the real transaction and the wine is the occasion for it. The exchange minted it as the coin of the warm drink that makes the cold bearable.",
