      "SAKURA2 is the Token Game's most geographically mobile March coin. The sakura zensen — the cherry blossom front that travels northward across Japan each spring, arriving in Kagoshima in late March and reaching Sapporo in late April — carries in The Stash a 'moving front mechanic' where SAKURA2 yield migrates between nations in The Stash's 13-nation map as the seasonal cycle progresses, following the bloom northward.",
    utility:
      "SAKURA2 yield is highest in the nation currently experiencing peak bloom according to The Stash's seasonal front tracker — traders who hold SAKURA2 in the correct nation at the correct time earn the peak-bloom multiplier, while those in the wrong nation earn only the base rate. The coin rewards those who follow the front, not those who stay in one place.",
